{"full":"hf:hmellor/transformers-modeling-backend-for-vllm","spaceId":"hmellor/transformers-modeling-backend-for-vllm","name":"How a Transformers Model Loads in vLLM","source":"huggingface","description":"Animated walkthrough of vLLM's Transformers modeling backend","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"HTML","topics":["static","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":6,"created":"2026-07-08T14:51:38.000Z","updated":"2026-09-22T14:31:21.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://hmellor-transformers-modeling-backend-for-vllm.static.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/hmellor/transformers-modeling-backend-for-vllm","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:56:13.247Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T13:56:13.247Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T13:56:13.247Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🧠","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An animated, self-contained walkthrough — built to present at conferences — of what happens when you vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct-FP8 --model-impl transformers using the Transformers modeling backend. It follows the control flow from the CLI, through backend-class resolution and the MRO, into Base.init rebuilding the model, and then sends a batch through — watching execution hop back and forth across the vLLM ⇄ Transformers boundary at the attention and MoE seams.","Qwen3-VL-FP8 (a multimodal, FP8-quantized MoE) is used because it exercises more of the backend than a plain text model: the multimodal path (TransformersMultiModalMoEForCausalLM + vision tower + M-RoPE), FP8 quantization through SupportsQuant, pipeline-parallel deletions (the Base.init walk-through is shown at PP=2), the fuser system (QKV / RMSNorm / MoE), and the fact that a native vLLM implementation exists, so the backend must be explicitly requested."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/hmellor/transformers-modeling-backend-for-vllm/blob/main/README.md","fi